  "description_short": "French-style bakery and café serving artisan breads, pastries, and all-day breakfasts in the heart of Plett.",
  "description_long": "Tucked into The Lookout Centre on Plettenberg Bay's main road, Le Fournil brings a slice of French baking tradition to the Garden Route. The aroma of freshly baked croissants and sourdough loaves greets you at the door, while the display case tempts with pain au chocolat, quiches, and seasonal tarts. It's the kind of place where locals pop in for their morning coffee and visitors linger over breakfast platters piled with fresh pastries.\n\nThe café side offers all-day breakfast options, decent espresso, and light lunches that lean on quality ingredients rather than fuss. Seating spills between the indoor dining area and a small courtyard, perfect for a relaxed morning catch-up or a quick bite between beach visits. The adjoining art gallery adds a touch of browsing interest if you're waiting for a table.\n\nIt's straightforward, honest café fare done well, with that unmistakable bakery warmth that makes it a reliable stop whether you're after a proper breakfast, a takeaway loaf for your holiday house, or just a good flat white and something sweet.",
